description = [=[mod id 3426836832

[h1]Blast to the Past (B2TP)[/h1]

A vanilla-flavored Natural Selection 2 mod aimed balancing the game 6v6 to 8v8 conditions, the original intended size of public play of ns2, back to the time where 8v8 servers were commonplace.

While stats on ns2panel.com show an almost 50-50 winrate (which is a good thing), in our experience most players have a higher marine than alien hiveskill, a rare 5 sight years ago.

As a consequence, the hive skill system, using the per-team-hiveskills feature that didn't exist back them can simply solve these imbalances by slightly stacking the alien team with better players. This, in turn, creates a 50-50 winrate.
However, if teams were to be sweapped then it would be expected the stronger,team would crush the opposition.

In conclusion, while the game can be 'balanced' for single rounds, it's not truly balanced until a 50-50-ish winrate is achieved after teamswaps.

This mod aims to attack the causes of this, by doing the least amount of changes whenever possible in the most impactful places. Most of these changes revert some values to what were vanilla values years ago, or were present in older or present compmod versions.

[hr][/hr]

[h1]ALIENS[/h1]

[h3]Lifeforms[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Lerk health[/b] 180 -> 170
[*][b]Lerk spike damage[/b] 10 -> 11
[*][b]Leap energy[/b] 45 -> 55
[*][b]Boneshield HP[/b] 1000 -> 600 [i](1000 was balanced for 10v10)[/i]
[*][b]Stomp energy[/b] 30 -> 45 [i](curbs stomp spam when the alien team has no adrenaline or a shift to sustain it)[/i]
[/list]

[h3]Fade[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Advanced Swipe[/b] new at Biomass 8 -- +8% swipe damage, 30 Tres, 90 second research. This will kill a marine on armor 2 in three swipes. Countered by armor 3
[*][b]Stab energy[/b] 30 -> 25
[*][b]Stab research[/b] 25 -> 20 Tres
[/list]

[h3]Upgrades[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Skulk Vampirism[/b] 4.66% -> 3.77% per shell [i](compmod change)[/i]. Vampirism also works on Exos now
[*][b]Aura[/b] no longer reveals health
[/list]

[h3]Chamber hive passives[/h3]
Chambers get their hive passives back:
[list]
[*][b]Shells[/b] regenerate themselves out of combat with a Crag hive
[*][b]Veils[/b] cloak themselves out of combat with a Shade hive
[*][b]Spurs[/b] can be picked up and moved by the commander with a Shift hive
[/list]

[h3]Cysts[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Build time[/b] 3.33 -> 6 seconds
[*][b]Shift hive build multiplier[/b] x1.25 -> x1.5 [i](compmod change, since vanilla cysting is broken in normal player counts)[/i]
[*][b]Flame damage[/b] split by source [i](compmod change)[/i]: welders x5 -> x4, flamethrowers x5 -> x7
[*][b]Mature cyst health[/b] 400 -> 300
[*][b]Detection range[/b] 8m -> 10m
[*][b]Drifters[/b] ordered onto an unbuilt cyst now queue up the whole chain behind it, instead of one cyst at a time
[/list]

[h3]Tunnels[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Gorges can drop tunnels[/b] 5 Pres per end, but only into a room whose power node is down, or onto infestation. They come up fully mature and spread infestation immediately
[*][b]Relocating[/b] 6 -> 5 Tres
[*][b]Minimap[/b] tunnel entrances are now labelled Entry 1-4 and Exit 1-4 on the map
[/list]

[h3]Hallucinations[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Biomass health[/b] removed -- hallucinations no longer get tougher as biomass rises
[*][b]Abilities[/b] can no longer use Umbra, Spores or Stomp
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]MARINES[/h1]

[h3]Round start[/h3]
Marines start with 1 IP (vanilla!) but
[list]
[*][b]7v7[/b] +5 Tres
[*][b]8v8[/b] +10 Tres
[/list]
This serves as an interpolation between 1IP and no bonuses for 6v6 (vanilla behavior) and +1 IP for the arcade clusterfugg that is 10v10, which is essentially +20 Tres. The only way to give "half an IP" is to give Tres. Giving a straight IP for 8v8 ammounts to nonstop early marine pressure and can snowball easily into marines choking out the aliens.

[h3]Structures and units[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]ARC health[/b] 2600 hp / 400 armor -> 2100 hp / 500 armor, limited to 4
[*][b]MAC speed[/b] +15% out of combat
[*][b]MAC rollout speed[/b] 2 -> 5
[*][b]Sentry[/b] 5 -> 6 Tres
[*][b]Sentry Battery[/b] 10 -> 12 Tres
[/list]

[h3]Drops[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Welder drop[/b] 3 -> 2 Tres
[*][b]Mine drop[/b] 7 -> 5 Tres
[*][b]Dropped weapon stay time[/b] 16 -> 20 seconds
[/list]

[h3]Medpack Tech[/h3]
Marines get Medpack Tech #1 and #2, ported from ENSL CompMod seasons 13 and 14:
[list]
[*][b]Default[/b] heal 25/25, identical to vanilla
[*][b]Medtech #1[/b] unlocks in the command station, requires armory. Heal 30/20
[*][b]Medtech #2[/b] unlocks in the command station, requires AA and Medtech #1. Heal 40/10
[/list]
This makes medding scale as the round progresses, since vanilla meds are truly lacking in the end game.

[h3]Weapons[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Weapon upgrade scaling[/b] 7.84% (?!) -> 10% per level, for all weapons including shotgun, FT and GL [i](a W3 shotgun meatshot goes from 210 to 221 damage)[/i]
[*][b]Shotgun falloff start[/b] 5m -> 7.5m
[*][b]Shotgun falloff end[/b] 15m -> 17.5m [i](where it does 50% damage)[/i]
[/list]
The shotgun change is half of the compmod change. Vanilla shotguns aren't terrible now. There's a reason the 10v10 meta skips them over entirely for AA.]=]
